In a broader cultural context, regicide can also refer to the killing of an emperor or any other reigning sovereign. The concept has been explored in various cultures and historical periods, including the ritual of killing a king at the end of his 7-year rule in some ancient cultures, which can be seen as a metaphor for the public's treatment of celebrities when their popularity fades.

