What are the standard durations of musical notes in relation to the semibreve and crochet?
According to the context, the standard durations of musical notes in relation to the semibreve (whole note) and crotchet (quarter note) are:

* Semibreve (whole note): 2 semibreves = 1 crotchet (quarter note)
* Crotchet (quarter note): 2 crotchets = 1 semibreve (whole note)
* Eighth note: 2 eighth notes = 1 crotchet (quarter note), and 1 eighth note = 1/2 crotchet (quarter note)
* Sixteenth note: 2 sixteenth notes = 1 eighth note, and 4 sixteenth notes = 1 crotchet (quarter note)
